    "question": {
      ":question/id": "c031f437-d43a-5602-99db-4b68d66860e6",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 9 & -8 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}$ on $A?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2}$ means that we need to multiply the second row of the matrix by $2.$\n\nMultiplying the second row by $2$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 6 & 4 & -6 \\\\ 9 & -8 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{2}:=2{R}_{2} \\\\ & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 2\\cdot (6) & 2\\cdot (4) & 2\\cdot (-6) \\\\ 9 & -8 & -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 & -9 \\\\ 12 & 8 & -12 \\\\ 9 & -8 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
