    "question": {
      ":question/id": "19059d49-64e0-5f66-9dbc-ca882f481f70",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the matrix $A,$ given by\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -9 & 8 \\\\ 6 & -6 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat matrix results from carrying out the row operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}$ on $A?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The operation ${R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2}$ means that we need to multiply the second row of the matrix by $\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nMultiplying the second row by $\\frac{1}{3}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -9 & 8 \\\\ 6 & -6 & -6 \\\\ -3 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\quad {R}_{2}:=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\ & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -9 & 8 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (6) & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-6) & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-6) \\\\ -3 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ & \\sim \\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -9 & 8 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 0 & -6\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
